      "translations": {
        "en": "As for what Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated from Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan ibn Rashid who said: I asked al-Askari (peace be upon him) in al-Madinah about a man who bequeathed wealth in the way of God, so he said, 'The way of God is our Shiah,' so this does not contradict the first report because it is possible to reconcile them according to what Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Babawayh al-Qummi (may God have mercy on him) mentioned, for he said, 'It is appropriate that the wealth be given to a man from the Shiah so that he performs Hajj with it, thus fulfilling both aspects. This is a close interpretation and does not contradict that.'"
